{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Distances\/documentation\/Distances\/Eccentricities"],"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Distances\/documentation\/Distances\/GraphProtocols"],"title":"Extended Modules","generated":true,"anchor":"Extended-Modules"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","title":"Distances","externalID":"Distances","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"Distances"}],"roleHeading":"Framework"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Distances\/documentation\/Distances","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/distances"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Distances/documentation/Distances":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Distances\/documentation\/Distances","url":"\/documentation\/distances","title":"Distances"},"doc://Distances/documentation/Distances/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Distances\/documentation\/Distances\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/distances\/graphprotocols","role":"collection","abstract":[]},"doc://Distances/documentation/Distances/Eccentricities":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Eccentricities"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Eccentricities"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every vertex’s eccentricity, computed once (Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"all_eccentricities"},{"type":"text","text":"), with the measures"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that follow from them: the radius (the least), the diameter (the greatest), the center and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the periphery (the vertices that attain them). An eccentricity is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":", standing for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"infinity, when some vertex is not reachable from the vertex; so the diameter is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the graph is not connected (or not strongly connected), and the radius when no vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaches every vertex."}],"url":"\/documentation\/distances\/eccentricities","identifier":"doc:\/\/Distances\/documentation\/Distances\/Eccentricities","title":"Eccentricities"}}}